---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Privacy policy" description="What information Scam-Proof Money collects (almost none), how visitor statistics and Google ads work, and how to opt out.">
  <div class="page">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="meta">Last updated: 23 November 2026</p>

    <p class="lead">Short version: this site has no accounts, no sign-up forms and no comment sections. We don't ask for personal information.</p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>
      We don't collect names, email addresses, phone numbers or payment details through this site. The
      "Is it a scam?" checker works entirely in your browser. What you choose is never sent to us or anyone else.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you email us, we receive your email address and whatever you write. We use it only to reply, and we
      never sell or share it.
    </p>

    <h2>Stored on your device</h2>
    <p>
      If you change the text size, your browser remembers your choice on your own device so the setting
      is still there next time. You can clear it at any time by clearing your browser's site data.
    </p>

    <h2>Our host</h2>
    <p>
      This site is hosted by Cloudflare. Like most web hosts, Cloudflare may process technical information
      such as your IP address and browser type to deliver pages and keep the site secure. See
      <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Videos and other sites</h2>
    <p>
      Some guides include a YouTube video. We use YouTube's privacy-enhanced embed, which limits tracking until
      you press play. When you play a video, YouTube may collect information under
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Google's privacy policy</a>. If you click a
      link to YouTube, Facebook or another site, that site's own policy applies.
    </p>

    <h2>Visitor statistics</h2>
    <p>
      We use <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/" rel="noopener">Cloudflare Web Analytics</a> to count
      visits and see which pages are useful, how fast they load, and which websites sent visitors here. It sets no
      cookies and stores nothing on your device, and Cloudflare says it does not fingerprint visitors using their IP
      address or browser details. We only see totals, never who you are.
    </p>

    <h2>Advertising</h2>
    <p>
      This site uses, or will soon use, Google AdSense to show ads. The ads help keep every guide and the Family
      Protection Kit free.
    </p>
    <ul class="plain">
      <li>Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on your previous visits to this website or other websites.</li>
      <li>Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to you based on your visits to this site and/or other sites on the internet.</li>
      <li>You can opt out of personalised advertising by visiting Google's <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" rel="noopener">Ads Settings</a>. You can also opt out of some other vendors' use of cookies for personalised advertising at <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="noopener">aboutads.info</a>.</li>
      <li>Visitors in the UK, the European Economic Area and Switzerland will be asked for consent before ad cookies are used, and can change their choice at any time.</li>
      <li>Learn more in <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>This site is written for adults and families. We don't knowingly collect information from children.</p>

    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>See our <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
